; MEXT: Matcha EXTension notation。書式は mext の docs/mext.md（スキルでは references/mext.md）を参照。

[ai]
; AI（または人）の判断。各行の ; 以降に理由を書く。
;   same "代表の文言" "同じ意味の文言"
;   neg  "文言A" "文言B"        … B は A の否定
;   failure "文言" / effect "文言" … 結論を「不成立からの帰結」「成立の効果」と読む
;   review "事実@評価" ok|doubtful|reject
;   concern 名 "前提" "前提" …    … 内容の上で一つの争点を共有する前提（感度分析でまとめて外す）
;   distinct "前提" "前提" …      … 内容の上で互いに独立な前提
;   connective "主張のラベルか要件の文言" 明示|読み … 結び方（AND/OR）が原文に明示されているか
;   fact-kind "事実" 記述|仮定|確認済み|著者の主張 … W の事実の種別
; --- negation
neg "a car-free center would hurt local shops〔local shops〕" "a car-free center could help local shops rather than hurt them〔local shops〕"   ; the business conclusion says "rather than hurt them" and is offered as the answer ("But") to the shop owners' fear (para 3)
; --- connectives (transcription judgment, car_free_op.matcha.md §3)
connective "plan" 読み   ; transcription judgment (car_free_op.matcha.md §3): "For these reasons" gathers the three reasons but does not say whether each one is needed
connective "L9" 読み     ; transcription judgment (car_free_op.matcha.md §3): the two injury facts are joined by "and" in one sentence; the evaluation needs both
connective "air" 読み    ; transcription judgment (car_free_op.matcha.md §3): para 4 lists two facts joined by "and" and states no inference
; --- fact kinds (transcription judgment, car_free_op.matcha.md §3)
fact-kind "downtown core" 記述   ; transcription judgment (car_free_op.matcha.md §3): the object of the claims
fact-kind "local shops" 記述     ; transcription judgment (car_free_op.matcha.md §3): the object of the claims
fact-kind "most serious pedestrian injuries in our city happen in the downtown core" 記述   ; transcription judgment (car_free_op.matcha.md §3): stated as fact (the op-ed's note says its figures are illustrative)
fact-kind "nearly all of them involve private cars" 記述   ; transcription judgment (car_free_op.matcha.md §3): stated as fact
fact-kind "shop owners fear that customers who drive will stop coming" 記述   ; transcription judgment (car_free_op.matcha.md §3): reported as fact
fact-kind "surveys in other cities suggest that pedestrians visit shops more often and spend about the same per month compared with drivers" 記述   ; transcription judgment (car_free_op.matcha.md §3): reported as fact; the surveys are not named
fact-kind "the nitrogen dioxide levels on our main street regularly exceed the national guideline" 記述   ; transcription judgment (car_free_op.matcha.md §3): stated as fact
fact-kind "traffic is the largest source of nitrogen dioxide downtown" 記述   ; transcription judgment (car_free_op.matcha.md §3): stated as fact
fact-kind "people with disabilities depend on cars" 記述   ; transcription judgment (car_free_op.matcha.md §3): the objection's premise, conceded by the author ("a real concern")
fact-kind "permits for disabled drivers, delivery vehicles and emergency services can be kept" 著者の主張   ; transcription judgment (car_free_op.matcha.md §3): the author's proposal about the design of the plan, not a reported fact
; --- review of the evaluations
review "（most serious pedestrian injuries in our city happen in the downtown core & nearly all of them involve private cars）@the involvement of private cars in nearly all of the injuries shows that the cars cause the danger" ok   ; a pedestrian injured in a collision with a car is injured by the car; "involve" → "cause" is an ordinary reading. (Whether removing the cars removes the danger — displacement to other streets, to delivery vehicles or bicycles — is the claim's own step, see report §6)
review "shop owners fear that customers who drive will stop coming@the shop owners' fear is well founded" ok   ; the objection's own inference; it is plausible that customers who can no longer drive downtown come less, and the op-ed does not dispute it
review "surveys in other cities suggest that pedestrians visit shops more often and spend about the same per month compared with drivers@the survey results from other cities hold in our city and lost driving customers would be made up by pedestrian customers" doubtful   ; three leaps: (1) unnamed surveys in other cities are transferred to our city; (2) "suggest" is turned into a premise; (3) the surveys compare spending per customer, but the fear is about the number of customers — that drivers who stop coming are replaced by pedestrians is not shown
review "the nitrogen dioxide levels on our main street regularly exceed the national guideline@exceeding the national guideline shows a problem that calls for action" ok   ; regularly exceeding a national guideline is an accepted reason for action
review "traffic is the largest source of nitrogen dioxide downtown@private cars make up most of that traffic" doubtful   ; supplied premise (car_free_op.matcha.md §4): "traffic" includes buses, delivery vehicles and emergency services, and the op-ed itself keeps deliveries and emergency vehicles (para 5); diesel delivery and bus traffic can be a large share of NO2
review "permits for disabled drivers, delivery vehicles and emergency services can be kept@permits for disabled drivers would meet the needs of people with disabilities" doubtful   ; permits for disabled *drivers* do not cover people with disabilities who are driven by others or rely on taxis; and "can be kept" is a proposal (fact-kind 著者の主張), not a shown result

[extra]
;   fact "文言" / rule "a" & "b" -> "c" / default 名: "a" : "b" / "b" / priority 名1 > 名2

[claimed]
;   E1*: "文言", -"文言"   … 検証したい Extension（* は preferred であることも主張）
E1*: "the city council should adopt a car-free downtown plan〔downtown core〕", "safety", "business", "air", -"a car-free center would hurt local shops〔local shops〕", !"disability"   ; prior prediction from car_free_op.matcha.md §6 (copied, not newly made)

; ===== ここから下は mext.py が自動生成（手で直さない） =====
